reviews:
Each cake is around npr150, and the lemon tea at 30. The pudding was not too sweet and had a great base. The cheesecake seems to have had a similar base and was a bready-er kind of cheesecake, which was a rather unique but good we experience.

The place is very hippy and definitely for smokers but do not let that deter you (if you're a nonsmoker). Just sit by the door. ||| owner is mild and efficient; I don't understand why some reviews saying services not being good cos per my feeling he is wordless and kind.
iced latte is so cheap but with high quality which tastes similarly like the Frappuccino;
banana milk shake does taste healthy and pure;
coconut cake is mild sweet which suits me so perfectly;
pudding is obviously made with high percentages of eggs also mild sweet so is perfect.
some meaningful questions on the wall leading you a deep thinking.
Respect all these points. ||| Definitely among the top bakery / pastry shop in town. While it is among the oldest cafe in Kathmandu, it still has its charm. The glavours unique and extremely delicious and the prices would say quite cheap per slide even today. A must visit indeed. ||| I LOVED it here! Very chill atmosphere, tasty cake, and good tea.
I had coffee cake (100rupee) and hot tea (30rupee), the price is amazing too.
I also love the cigarette scent (used to smoke and now quit) so this place being smoker friendly is a plus for me too. ||| Very special cafe serving delicious cakes, tea and coffee in quirky, smoky and possibly rebellious environment! Their apple crumble is divine. Loved the alternative atmosphere!
